      "title": "Remote Code Execution via Mock API Parameter Injection",
      "descriptions": [
        {
          "lang": "en",
          "value": "An input validation flaw in MockServer Engine v4.2.0 through v4.5.2 allows remote unauthenticated attackers to pass malicious payloads via the custom routing configuration interface. Exploitation can lead to arbitrary command execution on the host operating system."
        }
      ],
      "affected": [
        {
